askAttribution: the code is a reply's message (R82 1b), a same-connection finished ask, bounded memory, restarts

Review follow-ups. A reply-first entry carries the result code as its message,
as R82 1b decided, and every entry pins side, code and detail. A new case reuses
a finished ask's connection for the next ask, so a per-connection recycler
fails too. The note and RESUME-CAPTURE.md say an attach answers every pending
ask, a Stop forgets them, and an app may forget its oldest unanswered asks past
a bound. Ids are never reused after an app restart either.

